Copyright and database rights
=============================

Copyright (c) 2026 Ancient Trees (ancienttrees.app). All rights reserved.

This repository carries no open-source licence and none is implied by it
being public. No permission is granted to copy, redistribute, adapt or
build upon the contents, in whole or in substantial part, for any purpose.
Reading it is fine. Reusing it is not, unless you ask and we say yes.

Two separate rights apply here, and the second is the one that matters most.

1. COPYRIGHT covers everything written: the tree stories, the page copy, the
   collection and species and country introductions, the source code, the
   design, and the documents in this repository. That protection is
   automatic and does not depend on any notice.

2. THE DATABASE RIGHT (Directive 96/9/EC, and in the Netherlands the
   Databankenwet) covers the collection itself. It exists because obtaining,
   verifying and presenting these records took a substantial investment, and
   it protects that investment separately from the individual facts. Every
   tree here was verified against at least two independent sources, given a
   located pin with a stated precision, and checked for whether it is still
   alive and still reachable. That work is the asset.

   Extracting or re-using a substantial part of the database, or repeatedly
   extracting insubstantial parts in a way that adds up to the same thing,
   requires our permission. This applies to the published feeds under
   /api/ exactly as it applies to the pages.

WHAT IS NOT OURS, AND WHAT WE DO NOT CLAIM

A fact about a tree is not ours. That an oak stands in a named park, its
species, its girth, its age: nobody owns those, including us. What is
protected is the collection, the verification and the writing around them.

Photographs on the site belong to their photographers and carry their own
open licences and credits, recorded per photograph. Nothing here overrides
those; they travel with the photograph.

Official tree registers used in our research keep their own licences, which
are listed with their attribution at https://ancienttrees.app/sources.
Where a register is published under an open licence, that licence governs
that register's own data, not our records about it.

Map tiles, map data and walking routes come from OpenFreeMap, OpenMapTiles,
OpenStreetMap contributors and Valhalla via FOSSGIS, under their own terms,
credited in the footer of every page.

WHAT YOU SEND US

If you send us a photograph, a tree or a correction, you keep it. The terms
of that exchange are at https://ancienttrees.app/terms and they are short.

ASKING

Research, teaching, a conservation body, a link, a quote with attribution:
ask, and the answer is usually yes. info@ancienttrees.app
